1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
 I also can add up reference images, right?

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,820
 So a reference image is something

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:10,300
 that we want to include in the generated image.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,980
 So for example, a logo or something like that, right?

5
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:16,700
 Or we can add a reference image and our prompt

6
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:20,380
 can be all about editing the very image that we gave it, right?

7
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:25,380
 So this is how we can edit our images with photorei.

8
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:26,660
 It's very easy.

9
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,620
 You just upload your image over here.

10
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:31,260
 So it can be an image of you, for example, right?

11
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:34,660
 Or an image containing you and a crowd of people.

12
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:37,540
 And then you explain to it that, for example,

13
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:40,980
 you want all everybody to be blurred, you know?

14
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,940
 Or you want everybody to be removed from the image, right?

15
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:47,580
 Or any kind of edit that you want to add to that very image.

16
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:52,220
 And by clicking generate, you'll be able to get the very image

17
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:55,380
 that you gave it as a reference image just

18
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:58,420
 with the edit additions, you know, and with the changes

19
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:00,700
 that you wanted to make.

20
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:01,620
 And that's pretty much all.

21
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:05,140
 I don't want to add any kind of reference images for now.

